---
import ArticleImage from "@/components/ui/ArticleImage.astro";

import oldTownCobblestone from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-old-town-cobblestone-street.webp";
import oldTownStreetScene from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-old-town-street-scene.webp";
import oldTownKnight from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-old-town-medieval-knight.webp";
import koukosRestaurant from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-koukos-restaurant.webp";
import koukosBreakfast from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-koukos-breakfast.webp";
import dreamCream from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-dream-cream.webp";
import symiHarbour from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/symi-island-colourful-harbour.webp";
import symiShopfront from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/symi-town-colourful-shopfront.webp";
import symiStreetCafes from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/symi-town-street-cafes.webp";
import symiArchitecture from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/symi-traditional-architecture.webp";
import symiYialaBeach from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/symi-yiala-beach.webp";
import symiYialaBeach2 from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/greece-symi-yiala-beach.webp";
import lindosTraditionalStreet from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-lindos-village-traditional-street.webp";
import lindosWhitewashedStreet from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-lindos-village-whitewashed-street.webp";
import lindosExploring from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-exploring-lindos-village.webp";
import stPaulsBay from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-lindos-st-paul's-bay.webp";
import stPaulsBayBeach from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-lindos-st-paul's-bay-beach.webp";
import lindosSunriseViewpoint from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-lindos-sunrise-viewpoint.webp";
import lindosAcropolis from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-lindos-akropolis.webp";
import kallitheaEntrance from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-kallithea-springs-entrance.webp";
import kallitheaSprings from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-kallithea-springs.webp";
import kallitheaBeachView from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-kallithea-springs-beach-view.webp";
import anthonyQuinnBay from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-anthony-quinn-bay.webp";
import kounnaRestoBar from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-kounna-beach-resto-bar.webp";
import kounnaCoffeeView from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-kounna-beach-coffee-with-view.webp";
import myrovolosRestaurant from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-myrovolos-restaurant.webp";
import myrovolosMezedopoleion from "@/assets/articles/rhodos-images/rhodes-myrovolos-restaurant-mezedopoleion.webp";

const prose = "article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0";
---

<section id="section-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 1: Rhodes Old Town &amp; Mandraki Harbour</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Explore Rhodes Old Town</h4>
    <p>I would recommend starting your first day in Rhodes by exploring Rhodes Old Town, one of the best-preserved medieval towns in Europe and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.</p>
    <p>What stood out most to me wasn't a specific attraction, but the atmosphere of the Old Town itself. Walking through the cobblestone streets, passing historic buildings, impressive stone gates, and small local shops genuinely felt like stepping back in time. Many of the buildings, signs, and hotels still reflect the town's medieval heritage, which gives the entire area a character unlike anywhere else on the island.</p>
    <p>I personally started my walk from Saint John's Gate, one of the entrances to the Old Town, before slowly making my way through the medieval streets. Take your time wandering through the side streets and seeing where they lead, and make sure not to miss the Street of the Knights, one of the most famous streets in Rhodes, as well as the area around the Palace of the Grand Master, which remains one of the town's most impressive landmarks.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={oldTownCobblestone} alt="Cobblestone street in Rhodes Old Town" caption="Rhodes Old Town — a UNESCO-listed medieval centre" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={oldTownStreetScene} alt="Street scene in the medieval streets of Rhodes Old Town" caption="Wandering the medieval streets" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>Near the Palace area, I even came across someone dressed as a medieval knight, which added an extra touch to the whole experience and made the city's history feel even more alive.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={oldTownKnight} alt="A person dressed as a medieval knight in Rhodes Old Town" caption="A medieval knight near the Palace of the Grand Master" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Koukos</h4>
    <p>After a morning of exploring, head to Koukos for lunch.</p>
    <p>This quickly became one of my favourite places to eat in Rhodes. The menu offers everything from breakfast and brunch to lunch and dinner, making it a great option at almost any time of day. I personally stopped by for both breakfast and lunch on different occasions and had a great experience each time.</p>
    <p>The setting feels relaxed and welcoming, making it the perfect place to take a break before continuing your day.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={koukosRestaurant} alt="Koukos restaurant in Rhodes" caption="Koukos" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={koukosBreakfast} alt="Breakfast served at Koukos in Rhodes" caption="A relaxed lunch stop" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Walk to Mandraki Harbour</h4>
    <p>From Rhodes Old Town, make your way towards Mandraki Harbour for a walk along the waterfront.</p>
    <p>This historic harbour is one of the most recognisable areas of Rhodes and is home to the famous windmills that overlook the sea. Even if you don't spend long here, it's a pleasant area to stroll around, especially later in the afternoon when the temperatures are a little more comfortable.</p>
    <p>The walk offers a completely different side of Rhodes compared to the medieval atmosphere of the Old Town, combining sea views, historic landmarks, and a more relaxed coastal setting.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Dinner at Stávlos</h4>
    <p>For dinner, I would recommend Stávlos.</p>
    <p>This was one of the restaurants recommended to me by local friends from Rhodes, which is usually a good sign when choosing where to eat. Known for its grilled meats and traditional Greek cuisine, it's a great place to end your first day on the island.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Optional: Dream Cream</h4>
    <p>If you're not quite ready to end the evening, consider stopping by Dream Cream for dessert.</p>
    <p>Whether you're in the mood for gelato, waffles, or pancakes, it's the perfect excuse for one last treat before calling it a day.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={dreamCream} alt="Dessert from Dream Cream in Rhodes" caption="Dream Cream — one last treat to end the day" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 2: Symi Island Day Trip</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Take the Ferry to Symi</h4>
    <p>If you're spending 5 days in Rhodes, I think Symi is one of the best day trips you can add to your itinerary.</p>
    <p>When planning my trip, I was deciding between Symi and Halki, as both islands are frequently recommended by locals as day trips from Rhodes. In the end, I chose Symi — and as soon as the ferry started approaching the harbour, I knew I had made the right choice.</p>
    <p>The moment the ferry begins approaching the harbour, it's almost impossible to stop taking photos. The colourful houses climbing up the hillside create one of the most beautiful arrivals I've experienced on a Greek island, and honestly, I don't think photos fully capture how impressive it looks in person.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={symiHarbour} alt="The colourful harbour of Symi island with houses climbing the hillside" caption="Arriving into Symi's colourful harbour" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Wander Through the Streets of Symi</h4>
    <p>Before heading anywhere specific, spend some time simply exploring the harbour area and wandering through the small streets.</p>
    <p>One of the things I loved most about Symi was how photogenic the entire island felt. Around almost every corner, you'll find colourful buildings, traditional architecture, and beautiful sea views that make you want to stop and take another photo. Rather than rushing straight to the beach, I would recommend allowing yourself a little time to explore first and soak up the atmosphere.</p>
    <div class="my-5 grid grid-cols-5 items-start gap-3 md:my-8 md:gap-4">
      <div class="col-span-3">
        <ArticleImage src={symiArchitecture} alt="Traditional architecture in Symi Town" caption="Traditional Symi architecture" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-2 flex flex-col gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage src={symiShopfront} alt="A colourful shopfront in Symi Town" caption="Colourful shopfronts around every corner in Symi" figureClass="m-0" />
        <ArticleImage src={symiStreetCafes} alt="Street cafes in Symi Town" caption="Cafes lining the streets of Symi" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Stop by The Panormitis Bakery (Gialos Branch)</h4>
    <p>If you're looking for a quick local snack, stop by The Panormitis Bakery (Gialos Branch) while you're exploring the town.</p>
    <p>It's a popular spot for traditional baked goods and savoury pies, making it an easy stop before continuing your day. If you're anything like me, you'll probably struggle to leave with just one thing.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Relax by the Sea</h4>
    <p>After exploring Symi Town, spend the rest of the afternoon by the sea.</p>
    <p>I personally walked to Yiala Beach, about 30 minutes from the harbour, and it ended up being one of my favourite moments of the day. The water was incredibly clear, there were very few people around, and it felt like the perfect place to slow down after exploring the town.</p>
    <p>If Yiala feels a little too far, don't worry about reaching a specific beach. One of the things I loved about Symi was that there are plenty of beautiful swimming spots along the coastline, making it easy to stop wherever catches your eye and simply enjoy the afternoon.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={symiYialaBeach} alt="The clear water at Yiala Beach in Symi" caption="Yiala Beach — clear water and a quiet afternoon" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={symiYialaBeach2} alt="The coastline at Yiala Beach in Symi" caption="Plenty of quiet swimming spots along the coast" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Return to Rhodes</h4>
    <p>After a full day of exploring, swimming, and photographing one of the most beautiful islands in the Dodecanese, return to Rhodes in the evening and enjoy a relaxed night before continuing your itinerary.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 3: Discover Lindos Village &amp; St. Paul's Bay</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Explore Lindos Village</h4>
    <p>I would highly recommend spending at least one night in Lindos rather than visiting as a day trip. Out of all the places I visited in Rhodes, Lindos was probably the one that gave me the strongest Greek island feeling, with its white houses, narrow streets, and beautiful views around almost every corner.</p>
    <p>Spend the afternoon wandering through the whitewashed streets, exploring the small alleyways, and discovering hidden corners along the way. Once many of the day visitors leave, the village takes on a much calmer atmosphere, making it even more enjoyable to explore.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={lindosTraditionalStreet} alt="A traditional street in Lindos Village" caption="Traditional streets of Lindos" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={lindosWhitewashedStreet} alt="A whitewashed street in Lindos Village" caption="Whitewashed alleyways and hidden corners" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <ArticleImage src={lindosExploring} alt="Exploring the narrow streets of Lindos Village" caption="Wandering through Lindos once the day visitors leave" />

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Visit St. Paul's Bay</h4>
    <p>A short walk from the village brings you to St. Paul's Bay, one of the most beautiful beaches in Rhodes.</p>
    <p>The combination of crystal-clear water, dramatic cliffs, and views towards the Acropolis creates one of the most photogenic spots on the island. Whether you decide to swim or simply enjoy the scenery, it's a place worth slowing down and appreciating rather than rushing through.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={stPaulsBay} alt="St. Paul's Bay in Lindos with views towards the Acropolis" caption="St. Paul's Bay" />
      <ArticleImage src={stPaulsBayBeach} alt="The beach at St. Paul's Bay in Lindos" caption="Crystal-clear water at St. Paul's Bay" />
    </div>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Tambakio</h4>
    <p>If you're looking for somewhere to stop for lunch, consider Tambakio.</p>
    <p>Located directly on the beach at St. Paul's Bay, it's hard to imagine a better setting for a relaxed meal by the sea. Even if you only stop for a drink, the location alone makes it worth a visit while spending the day around Lindos.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Enjoy Lindos in the Evening</h4>
    <p>Staying overnight allows you to experience a quieter side of Lindos once many of the day visitors have left.</p>
    <p>The streets become noticeably calmer, making it the perfect time for an evening walk through the village. Take your time, enjoy dinner, and soak up the atmosphere before calling it a night.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 4: Sunrise, Acropolis &amp; Return to Rhodes Town</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Watch Sunrise Over Lindos</h4>
    <p>If you're willing to wake up early, sunrise is one of the most rewarding times to see Lindos.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={lindosSunriseViewpoint} alt="Sunrise viewpoint overlooking Lindos" caption="Sunrise over Lindos" imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover" />
    <p>Head to one of the viewpoints overlooking the village before sunrise and watch the first light reach the Acropolis and St. Paul's Bay. The soft morning light completely transforms the landscape and offers a very different experience from the busy daytime atmosphere.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Breakfast at Melia</h4>
    <p>After sunrise, grab breakfast at Melia.</p>
    <p>It's a relaxed place to start the morning before continuing your day, and its rooftop garden offers lovely views towards Lindos and the Acropolis.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Visit the Acropolis of Lindos</h4>
    <p>After breakfast, head up to the Acropolis before the temperatures begin to rise.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={lindosAcropolis} alt="The Acropolis of Lindos overlooking the village and coastline" caption="The Acropolis of Lindos" imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover" />
    <p>This is one of the most important archaeological sites in Rhodes, and visiting early makes the experience much more enjoyable during the summer months. The views from the top over Lindos, St. Paul's Bay, and the coastline are easily among the best on the island.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Return to Rhodes Town</h4>
    <p>After exploring the Acropolis, make your way back to Rhodes Town and enjoy a relaxed afternoon.</p>
    <p>Splitting Lindos across two days makes the experience feel far less rushed. Instead of trying to fit everything into a few hours, you'll have time to enjoy the village, the beach, sunrise, and the Acropolis at a much more comfortable pace.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Day 5: Kallithea Springs &amp; Anthony Quinn Bay</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <h4 class="mb-3 text-black">Visit Kallithea Springs</h4>
    <p>Start your final day in Rhodes at Kallithea Springs.</p>
    <div class="my-5 grid grid-cols-3 items-start gap-3 md:my-8 md:gap-4">
      <div class="col-span-2">
        <ArticleImage src={kallitheaEntrance} alt="The entrance to Kallithea Springs in Rhodes" caption="Kallithea Springs" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-1 flex flex-col gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage src={kallitheaSprings} alt="The Italian-inspired architecture of Kallithea Springs" caption="Italian-inspired architecture" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" figureClass="m-0" />
        <ArticleImage src={kallitheaBeachView} alt="The seaside setting and clear water at Kallithea Springs" caption="Crystal-clear waters" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" figureClass="m-0" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>Originally known for its thermal baths, today the site is best known for its beautiful architecture, seaside setting, and crystal-clear waters. The combination of Italian-inspired buildings, stone pathways, and coastal views makes it one of the most photogenic locations on the island.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Spend the Afternoon at Anthony Quinn Bay</h4>
    <p>From Kallithea Springs, continue to Anthony Quinn Bay, one of the most famous beaches in Rhodes.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={anthonyQuinnBay} alt="The turquoise water and rocky surroundings of Anthony Quinn Bay in Rhodes" caption="Anthony Quinn Bay" imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover" />
    <p>Known for its turquoise water and dramatic rocky surroundings, it's easy to understand why this bay has become one of the island's most photographed locations. Seeing it from above gave me a completely different appreciation for its colours and shape. If you're visiting during summer, I would recommend arriving earlier in the day, as the beach tends to get busier later on.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Lunch at Kounna</h4>
    <p>If you're looking for somewhere to stop for lunch or a drink, Kounna is an easy recommendation.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={kounnaRestoBar} alt="Kounna beach resto-bar above Anthony Quinn Bay" caption="Kounna" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={kounnaCoffeeView} alt="Coffee with a coastline view at Kounna" caption="Coffee with a view over the coastline" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>Perched above Anthony Quinn Bay, it offers beautiful views over the coastline and makes a great place to take a break between swims. Even if you only stop for a coffee, the setting alone makes it worth a visit.</p>

    <h4 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-black">Dinner at Myrovolos</h4>
    <p>For your final dinner in Rhodes, I would recommend Myrovolos.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={myrovolosRestaurant} alt="Myrovolos restaurant in Rhodes" caption="Myrovolos" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
      <ArticleImage src={myrovolosMezedopoleion} alt="Meze dishes at Myrovolos mezedopoleion in Rhodes" caption="A modern meze spread" imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover" />
    </div>
    <p>This modern meze restaurant was recommended to me by local friends from Rhodes, which is usually a good sign when choosing where to eat. My husband and I ordered several dishes to share and honestly couldn't pick a favourite. Every plate that arrived at the table was excellent.</p>
    <p>The atmosphere felt warm and welcoming, making it a lovely place to end your time on the island.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-faq" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>FAQ</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={`${prose} space-y-6`}>
    <div id="faq-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">1. Is 5 days enough in Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>Yes. Five full days is enough time to experience Rhodes Old Town, visit Lindos, take a day trip to Symi, and enjoy some of the island's most beautiful beaches without feeling rushed.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">2. How to get around Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>I would recommend renting a car, as it gives you the flexibility to explore the island at your own pace and easily reach places such as Lindos, Kallithea Springs, and Anthony Quinn Bay.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">3. Where should you stay in Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>For this itinerary, I would recommend staying in Rhodes Town and using it as your base for the trip. It's a convenient location for exploring the island while avoiding the hassle of changing accommodation.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">4. Is Lindos worth visiting?</h4>
      <p>Yes, absolutely. If there is one place in Rhodes that captures the classic Greek island atmosphere, it's Lindos.</p>
      <p>Between its whitewashed streets, beautiful beaches such as St. Paul's Bay and Lindos Beach, and the historic Acropolis overlooking the village, it combines some of the best experiences the island has to offer.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">5. Is Symi worth visiting?</h4>
      <p>If you have enough time in your itinerary, I think Symi is one of the best day trips you can take from Rhodes. The colourful harbour, beautiful swimming spots, and relaxed atmosphere make it feel completely different from Rhodes itself.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-5" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">6. What is the best time to visit Rhodes?</h4>
      <p>The best months to visit Rhodes are May, June, September, and October, when the weather is warm and sunny but generally more comfortable for sightseeing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-before" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Final Thoughts</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>Looking back, what surprised me most about Rhodes was how much variety the island offers.</p>
    <p>Within just a few days, I found myself wandering through medieval streets, exploring the colourful harbour of Symi, watching the sunrise over Lindos, and spending afternoons by some of the clearest water I've seen in Greece.</p>
    <p>If you're planning your first trip to Rhodes, I hope this itinerary helps you decide where to start.</p>
  </div>
</section>
